 about the rights of india's  minorities under the hindu nationalist  government hasn't it  uh yes it has and i will agree with what  i said it is the rule of law that is on  trial and i'll extend it to the fact  that it is quotes that are on trial  lately  see the democratic setup that is in  india that concern the courts become the  sentinel qv that is the custodian of the  constitution  um the minorities are protected by that  constitution and that constitution is  predicted by the courts but if the  courts look the other way or if they are  not actively  protecting minorities protecting those  who are endangered protecting those who  are obsessed  the situation will come to what it has  already come where anyone has the power  to heckle a muslim girl going to school  or going to college or if those voices  are raised those voices are shut down by  saying that uh  we also have a right to wear suffering  challenge i say no one is stopping you  from wearing that but you cannot take  away the light of a muslim woman to wear  wear that  hijab  so this is an attack on the identity  this is an attack  on the democratic and constitutional  setup of india  fatima we don't have a whole lot of time  left but let me just ask you do you  think that we're going to see these  protests and counter protests growing in  the weeks ahead  i think so i think so that in the last  few years if you remember 2020 the delhi  community violence the riots where  muslims were targeted at that point of  time it also started as uh you know a  bunch of people who support the  government to support the bjp starting  this counter protest against people who  were protesting muslims predominantly  protesting against the citizenship  amendment act um and that protest come  to protest it eventually snowballed or  was actively manufactured orchestrated  in such a way that it snowballs into a  right light situation in the national  capital um so i think until and unless  uh a court actively tries to i